        "t": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Swap screens for things your child can do on their own, at the times screens creep in most: bedtime, mealtimes, car journeys and the hour after school. Keep screens out of bedrooms and the hour before bed, agree a few simple family rules, and put your own phone away too.</p><p>The Department for Education's guidance for families (March 2026) suggests no more than one hour of screen time a day for 2 to 5 year olds, avoiding screens for under-2s except for shared activities, and swapping a programme before sleep for a bedtime story.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
