    "faq": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "item_01": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How can I reduce my kids' screen time?",
            "content": "<p>Start with the times screens creep in most: bedtime, mealtimes, car journeys and the hour after school. Keep screens out of bedrooms and the hour before bed, agree a few simple family rules, and give children things they can start on their own, such as books, building toys or an audiobook player. Putting your own phone away helps too.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_02": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How much screen time is too much for a child?",
            "content": "<p>For under-5s, the Department for Education's guidance (March 2026) suggests no more than an hour a day for 2 to 5 year olds, and avoiding screens for under-2s except for shared activities that encourage bonding and conversation. For older children it is less about a fixed number and more about screens not replacing sleep, play and time together. There is more in our guide <a href=\"/blogs/news/how-much-screen-time-is-too-much-a-simple-guide-for-parents\">How much screen time is too much?</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "item_03": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What can children do instead of screens?",
            "content": "<p>Anything they can start by themselves works best: reading, drawing, building, outdoor play, board games and listening to stories. See our ideas in <a href=\"/blogs/news/the-benefits-of-encouraging-screen-free-time\">The benefits of encouraging screen-free time</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_04": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does listening to an audiobook count as screen time?",
            "content": "<p>Not on a screen-free player. Voxblock has no display at all: your child puts an audiobook on the player and presses play, so there is nothing to watch or scroll.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_05": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What age is Voxblock for?",
            "content": "<p>Toddlers to teens. The player is made for children aged 3 and over, and most 3 year olds can choose and play a story on their own. Audiobooks run from picture books to unabridged novels.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_06": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does Voxblock need wifi?",
            "content": "<p>No. There is no wifi, no downloads and no subscription. Each story is stored inside its audiobook, so it works anywhere, including in the car or on holiday.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
